1. The natural numbers include zero for us.

2. Condition (1) can't be weakened, right? What about Condition (2)?

3. Why does it suffice to check only Lorentz cone ranks in the table
   for Proposition 8? That's not what Theorem 3 (now) says. The HR(3)
   example can be extended to e.g.

     K = HC(3) + L(4) + L(1) + L(1) ~ HC(3) + HR(3)

   but there is probably something special about HC(3) + L(n) that
   allows us to get away with only Lorentz factors.
